{
  "$comment": "The Feature Library's single source of truth, read by the website (app/models/finance/module_catalog.rb) and the apps (packages/shared-types/src/modules.ts). Names and descriptions are translation keys (config/locales/billie_modules.*.yml, clients/universal/src/i18n/modules.ts). Three separate questions, never mixed: (1) AVAILABILITY, per surface ('web' is the Rails website; 'app' is the universal client on macOS, Windows, iOS and Android): 'available' = built and its essential journey works there; 'coming_soon' = not built yet; 'unsupported' = built on another surface but not on this one. (2) ENABLED = can be used. It is derived, not stored: every module that is available on a surface is enabled there, for every account, new or old. There is no per-person switch that disables a feature. (3) SIDEBAR VISIBILITY = whether the module has a sidebar entry. Only this is a personal choice (Settings > Feature Library); 'default_sidebar_visible' applies until the person chooses. Hiding a module from the sidebar never blocks its pages, never changes or deletes data, and never stops processing (e.g. recurring entries still post). Settings is a system entry, not a module: always in the sidebar, never stored. Financial services removed from the product scope are not listed here and must not be added back.",
